### CanteenTransactionService API Tests
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5195
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### 1. Authentication — Get JWT Token
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### 2. Canteen Transaction (CANTEEDN_DACON)
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2.1 Record a canteen transaction
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/canteen-transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "companyCode": 1,
  "employeeSysId": 1001,
  "employeeType": "R",
  "swipeDate": "20240115",
  "itemCode": 100,
  "itemType": "F",
  "employeeContribution": 50.00,
  "employerContribution": 100.00,
  "canteenNumber": "C1",
  "itemQuantity": 2,
  "entryUser": 999,
  "entryDate": "20240115",
  "gradeCategory": "A01"
}

### 2.2 Get transaction by serial number
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/canteen-transactions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.3 Get transactions by employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/canteen-transactions/employee/1001?fromDate=20240101&toDate=20240131
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.4 Get transactions by company and date
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/canteen-transactions/company/1/date/20240115
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.5 Cancel a transaction
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/canteen-transactions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### 3. Daily Availed (CANTEEN_DAYWISE_AVAILED)
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3.1 Process daily availed record
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/daily-availed
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "companyCode": 1,
  "employeeSysId": 1001,
  "employeeType": "R",
  "swipeDate": "20240115",
  "itemCode": 100,
  "itemType": "F",
  "employeeContribution": 50.00,
  "employerContribution": 100.00,
  "canteenNumber": "C1",
  "itemQuantity": 1,
  "entryUser": 999,
  "entryDate": "20240115",
  "gradeCategory": "A01"
}

### 3.2 Get daily availed by serial number
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/daily-availed/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.3 Get daily availed by employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/daily-availed/employee/1001?fromDate=20240101&toDate=20240131
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.4 Get daily availed by company and date
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/daily-availed/company/1/date/20240115
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### 4. MIS Batch Submission (CANTEEN_MIS_SBT)
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4.1 Submit an MIS batch
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/mis-batch
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "companyCode": 1,
  "employeeNumber": "EMP001",
  "swipeTime": "2024-01-15T12:30:00",
  "itemCode": 100,
  "itemQuantity": 3,
  "batchDate": "2024-01-15T00:00:00",
  "batchNumber": 5001,
  "canteenNumber": "1",
  "gateNumber": "G01"
}

### 4.2 Get MIS batch by serial number
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/mis-batch/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.3 Get MIS batches by batch number
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/mis-batch/batch/5001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.4 Get pending MIS batches
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/mis-batch/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.5 Process an MIS batch
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/mis-batch/1/process
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.6 Fail an MIS batch
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/mis-batch/1/fail
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "reason": "Validation error: invalid item code"
}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### 5. Minimal API Endpoints (v2)
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5.1 Record transaction via minimal API
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/canteen-transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "companyCode": 1,
  "employeeSysId": 1002,
  "employeeType": "C",
  "swipeDate": "20240116",
  "itemCode": 200,
  "itemType": "B",
  "employeeContribution": 30.00,
  "employerContribution": 70.00,
  "canteenNumber": "C2",
  "itemQuantity": 1,
  "entryUser": 999,
  "entryDate": "20240116",
  "gradeCategory": "B02"
}

### 5.2 Get transaction via minimal API
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/canteen-transactions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### 6. Health Checks
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6.1 Full health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 6.2 Readiness check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### 6.3 Liveness check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### 7. GraphQL
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### 7.1 Query transaction by serial number
POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "query": "query { transactionBySerialNumber(serialNumber: 1) { serialNumber companyCode employeeSysId swipeDate itemCode itemQuantity employeeContribution employerContribution } }"
}

### 7.2 Query daily summary via Dapper
POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "query": "query { dailySummary(companyCode: 1, swipeDate: \"20240115\") { companyCode swipeDate itemCode itemDescription totalQuantity totalEmployeeContribution totalEmployerContribution } }"
}

### 7.3 Record transaction via GraphQL mutation
POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "query": "mutation { recordTransaction(input: { companyCode: 1, employeeSysId: 1003, employeeType: \"R\", swipeDate: \"20240117\", itemCode: 300, itemType: \"F\", employeeContribution: 40, employerContribution: 80, canteenNumber: \"C1\", itemQuantity: 1, entryUser: 999, entryDate: \"20240117\", gradeCategory: \"A01\" }) { serialNumber companyCode employeeSysId } }"
}
